  Local evidence:
    boundary-only local rows are AP and GW; their owner skeletons agree.
    positive-open rows are safe, but K33-labelled rows remain state-lift obligations.
    raw apex tournament and raw scalar M each forget a load-bearing label.
  Sharp theorem target:
    every primitive residual that is not discharged by q-threshold or Haar-open
    strictness must either be AP/GW boundary-only or construct the HYP-2908
    TournamentStateLift packet.
